"Micronesian (Pohnpei/Ponape Island, Caroline Islands) god of the coconut "
"palm."
msgstr "ミクロネシア (カロリン諸島のポンペイ/ポナペ島) のココヤシの神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Canelos Quichua (Ecuador) female spirit of the garden
#. soil and of pottery clay.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:652
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Nunghui"
msgstr "ヌングイ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:652
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Canelos Quichua (Ecuador) female spirit of the garden soil and of pottery "
"clay."
msgstr "カネロス・クチュア族 (エクアドル) の庭の土と陶土の女性精霊。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Scandinavian goddess who “Signifies the seed.”
#: data/nomenclature.fab:654
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Thrud"
msgstr "スルーズ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:654
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Scandinavian goddess who “Signifies the seed.”"
msgstr "「種を表す」スカンジナビアの女神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Egyptian god of rain.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:656
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Nepen"
msgstr "ネペン"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:656
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Egyptian god of rain."
msgstr "エジプトの雨の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Polish god of the fields, of the tilling.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:658
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Tawals"
msgstr "タヴァルス"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:658
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Polish god of the fields, of the tilling."
msgstr "ポーランドの畑と耕作の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Syrian god of agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:660
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Asari"
msgstr "アサリ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:660
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Syrian god of agriculture."
msgstr "シリアの農業の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Egyptian cobra-headed goddess of the harvest.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:662
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Ernutet"
msgstr "エルヌテト"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:662
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Egyptian cobra-headed goddess of the harvest."
msgstr "コブラの頭を持つエジプトの豊穣の女神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Italian agricultural god who watched over the
#. harvested and stored crop.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:664
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Consus"
msgstr "コンスス"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:664
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Italian agricultural god who watched over the harvested and stored crop."
msgstr "イタリアの農業の神、収穫され貯蔵された作物を見守る。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Greek god of agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:666
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Aristaeus"
msgstr "アリスタエウス"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:666
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Greek god of agriculture."
msgstr "ギリシャの農業の女神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Kogi (N. Colombia) god, who taught people
#. agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:668
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Duginavi"
msgstr "デュギナビ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:668
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Kogi (N. Colombia) god, who taught people agriculture."
msgstr "コーギ人 (コロンビア北部) の神、人々に農業を教えた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Paraguay, Brazil, and Bolivia spirit helpful in
#. gardening.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:670
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Hakumyi"
msgstr "ハクミイ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:670
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Paraguay, Brazil, and Bolivia spirit helpful in gardening."
msgstr "パラグアイ、ブラジル、ボリビアの園芸に役立つ精霊。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Latvian spirit, “Mother of the fields.”
#: data/nomenclature.fab:672
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Laukumate"
msgstr "ラウクマテ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:672
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Latvian spirit, “Mother of the fields.”"
msgstr "ラトビアの精霊、「畑の母」。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Aztec fertility god, associated with maize and
#. flowers; patron of music and dance.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:674
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Xochipilli"
msgstr "ショチピリ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:674
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Aztec fertility god, associated with maize and flowers; patron of music and "
"dance."
msgstr "アステカのトウモロコシと花に関連がある、豊穣の神。音楽と踊りの守護神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Veddan (Sri Lanka) goddess, provider of food (“Milk
#. mother”).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:676
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Kiriamma"
msgstr "キリアンマ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:676
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Veddan (Sri Lanka) goddess, provider of food (“Milk mother”)."
msgstr "ヴェッダ人 (スリランカ) の女神、食べ物の供給者 (「ミルクの母」) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Yurok (California, USA) dwarf god of acorns and the
#. distributor of vegetal abundance.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:678
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Megwomets"
msgstr "メグウォメツ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:678
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Yurok (California, USA) dwarf god of acorns and the distributor of vegetal "
"abundance."
msgstr "ユロック族 (米国カリフォルニア州) のドングリの小人の神で、豊富な野菜の分配者。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Yap Islands (Caroline Islands, Micronesia) guardian
#. of the taro fields who controls the yield of the crops.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:680
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Begbalel"
msgstr "ベグバレル"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:680
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Yap Islands (Caroline Islands, Micronesia) guardian of the taro fields who "
"controls the yield of the crops."
msgstr "ヤップ諸島 (ミクロネシアのカロリン諸島) の作物の収穫量をコントロールするタロイモ畑の守護者。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Mexican god/goddess of maize and agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:682
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Centeotl"
msgstr "センテオトル"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:682
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Mexican god/goddess of maize and agriculture."
msgstr "メキシコのトウモロコシと農業の神/女神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Nicaraguan god of cacao.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:684
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Cacaguat"
msgstr "カカグアト"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:684
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Nicaraguan god of cacao."
msgstr "ニカラグアのココアの神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); British god of the cultivated field and of the
#. meadows.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:686
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Ialonus"
msgstr "イアロヌス"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:686
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "British god of the cultivated field and of the meadows."
msgstr "ブリトン族の耕作地と牧草地の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Arabian tribal god worshipped as the provider of
#. food.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:688
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Razeka"
msgstr "ラゼカ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:688
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Arabian tribal god worshipped as the provider of food."
msgstr "食物を供給する者として崇拝されるアラビア部族の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Indian god of agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:690
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Hatipowa"
msgstr "ハティポワ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:690
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Indian god of agriculture."
msgstr "インドの農業の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Celtic god of malt.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:692
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Braciaca"
msgstr "ブラキアカ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:692
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Celtic god of malt."
msgstr "ケルトの麦芽の神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Korean Earth goddess who brought 5 grains to Jeju
#. island, and began agriculture.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:694
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Jacheongbi"
msgstr "ジャチョンビ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:694
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Korean Earth goddess who brought 5 grains to Jeju island, and began "
"agriculture."
msgstr "済州島に五穀をもたらし農耕を始めた朝鮮の大地の女神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Fijian serpent god of agriculture and the underworld.
#. He makes the breadfruit and other fruit trees blossom and yield fruit.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:696
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Ratumaibulu"
msgstr "ラトゥマイブル"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:696
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Fijian serpent god of agriculture and the underworld. He makes the "
"breadfruit and other fruit trees blossom and yield fruit."
msgstr "フィジーの農耕と冥界の蛇の神。パンノキや他の果樹に花を咲かせ、実を結ばせる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Udmurt (Volga-Ural Region, Russia) agricultural
#. festival after the spring sowing (June).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:698
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Gerber Catena"
msgstr "ゲルベル連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:698
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Udmurt (Volga-Ural Region, Russia) agricultural festival after the spring "
"sowing (June)."
msgstr "ウドムルト人 (ロシアのボルガ、ウラル地方) の春の種まき後の農業祭 (6月に行われる) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Brazilian festival with a rural theme held in June at
#. end of rainy season to give thanks for fertile rain.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:700
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Junina Catenae"
msgstr "ジュニナ連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:700
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Brazilian festival with a rural theme held in June at end of rainy season to"
" give thanks for fertile rain."
msgstr "豊かな雨に感謝し、雨期明けの6月に開催される田舎をテーマにしたブラジルのお祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Gaelic festival at the end of the harvest season. It
#. was observed in Ireland and Scotland during 7 days in October and November,
#. nearly halfway between the autumn equinox and the winter solstice.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:702
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Samhain Catenae"
msgstr "サムハイン連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:702
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Gaelic festival at the end of the harvest season. It was observed in Ireland"
" and Scotland during 7 days in October and November, nearly halfway between "
"the autumn equinox and the winter solstice."
msgstr "収穫期の終わりに行われるゲールのお祭り。アイルランドとスコットランドでは、秋分と冬至のほぼ中間にあたる10月から11月の7日間に行われた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Mordvinian (Volga River Region, Russia) agricultural
#. festival.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:704
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Baltay Catena"
msgstr "バルタイ連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:704
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Mordvinian (Volga River Region, Russia) agricultural festival."
msgstr "モルドヴィン人 (ロシア・ヴォルガ川流域) の農業の祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Tamil (Sri Lanka and S. India) harvest festival
#. observed in mid-January. It is a time for giving thanks to nature.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:706
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Pongal Catena"
msgstr "ポンガル連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:706
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Tamil (Sri Lanka and S. India) harvest festival observed in mid-January. It "
"is a time for giving thanks to nature."
msgstr "タミル (スリランカと南インド) の1月中旬に行われる収穫祭。自然に感謝する時期になる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Nigerian (Zuru Emirate, Kebbi State) harvest
#. festival.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:708
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Uhola Catenae"
msgstr "ウホラ連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:708
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Nigerian (Zuru Emirate, Kebbi State) harvest festival."
msgstr "ナイジェリア (ケビ州ズル首長国) の収穫祭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Festival of rice planting season at Sumba Island
#. (Lesser Sunda Islands, E. Indonesia). (February – March).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:710
msgctxt "facula"
msgid "Pasola Facula"
msgstr "パソラ白斑"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:710
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Festival of rice planting season at Sumba Island (Lesser Sunda Islands, E. "
"Indonesia). (February – March)."
msgstr "スンバ島 (インドネシア東部の小スンダ列島) の田植えシーズンの祭り。(2月から3月に開催) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); The major festival in Ancient Rome to celebrate for
#. the grain goddess Ceres (8 days in mid- to late April).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:712
msgctxt "facula"
msgid "Cerealia Facula"
msgstr "ケレアリア白斑"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:712 data/nomenclature.fab:764
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"The major festival in Ancient Rome to celebrate for the grain goddess Ceres "
"(8 days in mid- to late April)."
msgstr "穀物の女神ケレスを祝う古代ローマの大きな祭り (8月中旬から下旬に8日間開催) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Roman wine festivals, celebrated twice a year: on
#. April 23 when the new wine was tasted and August 19 when the new wine was
#. opened for all.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:714
msgctxt "facula"
msgid "Vinalia Faculae"
msgstr "ウィナリア白斑"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:714
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman wine festivals, celebrated twice a year: on April 23 when the new wine"
" was tasted and August 19 when the new wine was opened for all."
msgstr "年2回開催されるローマのワイン祭り。4月23日に新ワインの試飲が行われ、8月19日に新ワインが全員に開封される。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Bengal region (Bangladesh and West Bengal state in
#. India) “new rice” harvest festival.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:716
msgctxt "fossa"
msgid "Nabanna Fossa"
msgstr "ナバンナ地溝帯"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:716
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Bengal region (Bangladesh and West Bengal state in India) “new rice” harvest"
" festival."
msgstr "ベンガル地方 (バングラデシュとインドの西ベンガル州) の「新米」の収穫祭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Jewish autumn festival of double thanksgiving,
#. celebrated for 8 days in September – October.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:718
msgctxt "labes"
msgid "Sukkot Labes"
msgstr "スコット地滑り地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:718
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Jewish autumn festival of double thanksgiving, celebrated for 8 days in "
"September – October."
msgstr "ユダヤ教の秋の二重感謝祭で、9月から10月の8日間にわたって開催される。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Dutch (The Netherlands) day of thanksgiving for the
#. crop (1st Wednesday of November).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:720
msgctxt "labes"
msgid "Dankdag Labes"
msgstr "ダンクダフ地滑り地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:720
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Dutch (The Netherlands) day of thanksgiving for the crop (1st Wednesday of "
"November)."
msgstr "オランダの収穫の感謝祭の日 (11月の第1水曜日) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Harvest festival in Kerala, India, held in August-
#. September.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:722
msgctxt "labes"
msgid "Onam Labes"
msgstr "オナム地滑り地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:722
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Harvest festival in Kerala, India, held in August-September."
msgstr "インドのケララ州で8月から9月にかけて行われる収穫祭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Hawaiian harvest festival in honor of Lono, a god of
#. fertility, agriculture, and rainfall (lasts four months, from October
#. through February).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:724
msgctxt "labyrinthus"
msgid "Makahiki Labyrinthus"
msgstr "マカヒキ迷路地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:724
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Hawaiian harvest festival in honor of Lono, a god of fertility, agriculture,"
" and rainfall (lasts four months, from October through February)."
msgstr "豊穣、農業、降雨の神ロノを讃えるハワイの収穫祭 (10月から2月までの4か月間続く) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Sumi tribe (Nagaland, NE India) traditional post-
#. harvest festival, signifies the celebration of the seasons harvest’s
#. thanksgiving.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:726
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Ahuna Mons"
msgstr "アフナ山"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:726
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Sumi tribe (Nagaland, NE India) traditional post-harvest festival, signifies"
" the celebration of the seasons harvest’s thanksgiving."
msgstr "スミ族 (インド北東部ナガランド州) の伝統的な収穫後の祭り。収穫への感謝の季節を祝うことを意味する。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Ancient Roman festival to honor Liber and Libera,
#. deities of the vine, worshiped, along with Ceres as fertility gods, held on
#. March 17.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:728
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Liberalia Mons"
msgstr "リベラリア山"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:728
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Ancient Roman festival to honor Liber and Libera, deities of the vine, "
"worshiped, along with Ceres as fertility gods, held on March 17."
msgstr "3月17日に行われる、ブドウの神であり、ケレスとともに豊穣の神として崇拝されていたリベルとリベラを称える古代ローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Ecuadorian corn/maize festival (held in September).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:730
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Yamor Mons"
msgstr "ヤモル山"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:730
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Ecuadorian corn/maize festival (held in September)."
msgstr "エクアドルのトウモロコシの祭り (9月開催) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Grape harvest festival in Mendoza (Argentina) during
#. the first week of March. It is one of the most important festivals in the
#. country.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:732
msgctxt "planitia"
msgid "Vendimia Planitia"
msgstr "ヴェンディミア平原"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:732
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Grape harvest festival in Mendoza (Argentina) during the first week of "
"March. It is one of the most important festivals in the country."
msgstr "3月の第1週にメンドーサ (アルゼンチン) で行われるブドウ収穫祭。この国で最も重要な祭りの1つ。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Japanese cherry blossom festival.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:734
msgctxt "planum"
msgid "Hanami Planum"
msgstr "ハナミ高原"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:734
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Japanese cherry blossom festival."
msgstr "日本の桜祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Ga people (Ghana) harvest festival to celebrate all
#. local crops. Celebrations begin in May and culminate in August.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:736
msgctxt "regio"
msgid "Homowo Regio"
msgstr "ホモウォ地域"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:736
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Ga people (Ghana) harvest festival to celebrate all local crops. "
"Celebrations begin in May and culminate in August."
msgstr "ガ族 (ガーナ) の地元のすべての作物を祝う収穫祭。お祝いは5月に始まり、8月に最高潮に達する。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Hopi (SW USA) ritual ending the katsina (spiritual
#. beings) season, celebrates the katsinas’ return to their spiritual home in
#. July and their part in the blossoming of plant life.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:738
msgctxt "rupes"
msgid "Niman Rupes"
msgstr "ニマン断崖"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:738
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Hopi (SW USA) ritual ending the katsina (spiritual beings) season, "
"celebrates the katsinas’ return to their spiritual home in July and their "
"part in the blossoming of plant life."
msgstr "ホピ族（アメリカ南西部）のカチナ (精霊) の季節を終わらせる儀式、7月にカチナが精神的な故郷に戻り、植物の開花に貢献することを祝う。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Azerbaijani festival of pomegranate harvest. Held in
#. October – November in Goychay city, center of pomegranates cultivation in
#. Azerbaijan.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:740
msgctxt "sulcus"
msgid "Nar Sulcus"
msgstr "ナル溝"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:740
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Azerbaijani festival of pomegranate harvest. Held in October – November in "
"Goychay city, center of pomegranates cultivation in Azerbaijan."
msgstr "アゼルバイジャンのザクロ収穫祭。アゼルバイジャンのザクロ栽培の中心地ゴイチャイ市で10月から11月に開催される。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Celtic harvest festival, traditionally celebrated on
#. August 1.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:742
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Lughnasa Tholus"
msgstr "ルーナサ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:742
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Celtic harvest festival, traditionally celebrated on August 1."
msgstr "ケルトの収穫祭、伝統的に8月1日に行われる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Bon Dalien; Khmer (Cambodia) festival at the end of
#. the rice harvest (January – February).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:744
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Dalien Tholus"
msgstr "ダリエン円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:744
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Bon Dalien; Khmer (Cambodia) festival at the end of the rice harvest "
"(January – February)."
msgstr "ボン・ダリエン; クメール族 (カンボジア) の稲刈が終わった時の祭り (1月から2月) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Garo people (Meghalaya and Assam states, NE India,
#. and Bangladesh) post-harvest three-day festival that marks the end of the
#. agricultural year (in November).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:746
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Wangala Tholus"
msgstr "ワンガラ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:746
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Garo people (Meghalaya and Assam states, NE India, and Bangladesh) post-"
"harvest three-day festival that marks the end of the agricultural year (in "
"November)."
msgstr ""
"ガロ族 (インド北東部メガーラヤ州、アッサム州とバングラデシュ) の農作物の収穫後の3日間の祭り。農耕の1年の終わり (11月) を告げる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Colombian harvest festival, Fiestas de La Cosecha,
#. held in August at Pereira. (Cosecha means ‘harvest’ in Spanish).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:748
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Cosecha Tholus"
msgstr "コセチャ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:748
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Colombian harvest festival, Fiestas de La Cosecha, held in August at "
"Pereira. (Cosecha means ‘harvest’ in Spanish)."
msgstr "8月にペレイラで開催されるコロンビアの収穫祭「フィエスタ・デ・ラ・コセチャ」。(コセチャはスペイン語で「収穫」を意味する) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); African-American festival ("First Fruits") based on
#. ancient African harvest festivals (from December 26 to January 1).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:750
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Kwanzaa Tholus"
msgstr "クワンザ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:750
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"African-American festival (”First Fruits”) based on ancient African harvest "
"festivals (from December 26 to January 1)."
msgstr "古代アフリカの収穫祭に基づいたアフリカ系アメリカ人のお祭り (「ファースト フルーツ」) (12月26日から1 月1 日まで) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Quechua (Peru) harvest festival (in May). Aymuray
#. means “the song of the harvest”.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:752
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Aymuray Tholi"
msgstr "アイムライ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:752
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Quechua (Peru) harvest festival (in May). Aymuray means “the song of the "
"harvest”."
msgstr "ケチュア族 (ペルー) の収穫祭 (5月開催) 。アイムライは「収穫の歌」を意味する。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Hosil bayrami; Uzbek (Central Asia) cotton harvest
#. festival.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:754
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Hosil Tholus"
msgstr "ホシル円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:754
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Hosil bayrami; Uzbek (Central Asia) cotton harvest festival."
msgstr "ホシル・バイラミ; ウズベキスタン (中央アジア) の綿の収穫祭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Mikeldiena; Latvian harvest festival. Held at the end
#. of September.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:756
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Mikeli Tholus"
msgstr "ミケリ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:756
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Mikeldiena; Latvian harvest festival. Held at the end of September."
msgstr "ミケルディエナ; ラトビアの収穫祭。 9月末に開催される。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Belarusian harvest festival (21 September).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:758
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Bagach Tholus"
msgstr "バガチ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:758
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Belarusian harvest festival (21 September)."
msgstr "ベラルーシの収穫祭 (9月21日) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Punjabi (Pakistan, NW India) harvest festival. Held
#. on January 13.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:760
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Lohri Tholus"
msgstr "ローリー円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:760
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Punjabi (Pakistan, NW India) harvest festival. Held on January 13."
msgstr "パンジャブ地方 (パキスタン、インド北西部) の収穫祭。1月13日に行われる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); Finnish harvest festival (first Saturday of
#. November).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:762
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Kekri Tholus"
msgstr "ケクリ円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:762
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Finnish harvest festival (first Saturday of November)."
msgstr "フィンランドの収穫祭 (11月の第一土曜日)  。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Ceres); The major festival in Ancient Rome to celebrate for
#. the grain goddess Ceres (8 days in mid- to late April).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:764
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Cerealia Tholus"
msgstr "ケレアリア円錐丘"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Hero of humorous folktales told throughout the
#. Middle East, southern Europe and parts of Asia. Undertook numerous journeys
#. with his donkey, upon which he is seated facing backwards. Supposed to be
#. of a Turkish origin.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:766
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Nasreddin"
msgstr "ナスレッディン"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:766
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Hero of humorous folktales told throughout the Middle East, southern Europe "
"and parts of Asia. Undertook numerous journeys with his donkey, upon which "
"he is seated facing backwards. Supposed to be of a Turkish origin."
msgstr "中東、南ヨーロッパ、アジアの一部で語られるユーモラスな民話の英雄。ロバに後ろ向きに座って何度も旅をした。トルコ起源と思われる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Spaceship pilot, the main character in a series of
#. fictional stories by the Polish author Stanislaw Lem (1921–2006). He
#. travelled between the Earth, Moon and Mars.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:768
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Pirx"
msgstr "ピルクス"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:768
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Spaceship pilot, the main character in a series of fictional stories by the "
"Polish author Stanislaw Lem (1921–2006). He travelled between the Earth, "
"Moon and Mars."
msgstr ""
"宇宙船パイロット、ポーランドの作家スタニスワフ・レム (1921年-2006年) による一連のSF物語の主人公。地球、月、火星間を旅行した。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Hindu mythological princess, who traveled through
#. time and space in search of a suitor, described in the epic narrative
#. "Mahabharata".
#: data/nomenclature.fab:770
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Revati"
msgstr "レヴァティ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:770
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Hindu mythological princess, who traveled through time and space in search "
"of a suitor, described in the epic narrative “Mahabharata”."
msgstr "ヒンズー教神話に登場する王女、求婚者を求めて時空を旅した。叙事詩『マハーバーラタ』に描かれている。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Captain of the Nautilus, a submarine, in the novels
#. "Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea" (1870) and "The Mysterious Island"
#. (1874) by the French author Jules Verne (1825–1905). The stories recount
#. fantastical undersea travels and explorations.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:772
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Nemo"
msgstr "ネモ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:772
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Captain of the Nautilus, a submarine, in the novels “Twenty Thousand Leagues"
" Under the Sea” (1870) and “The Mysterious Island” (1874) by the French "
"author Jules Verne (1825–1905). The stories recount fantastical undersea "
"travels and explorations."
msgstr ""
"フランスの作家ジュール・ヴェルヌ (1825–1905) の小説 『海底二万里』(1870年) と『神秘の島』 (1874年) "
"に登場する潜水艦ノーチラス号の艦長。幻想的な海底旅行と探検についての物語。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); American fictional character, protagonist of "The
#. Wonderful Wizard of Oz" and other children’s novels, small girl who visited
#. the magical Land of Oz.
#. TRANSLATORS: (Venus); Greek first name.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:774 data/nomenclature.fab:28506
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Dorothy"
msgstr "ドロシー"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:774
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"American fictional character, protagonist of “The Wonderful Wizard of Oz” "
"and other children’s novels, small girl who visited the magical Land of Oz."
msgstr "アメリカの架空の人物、「オズの魔法使い」やその他の児童文学の主人公、魔法の国オズを訪れた小さな女の子。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Russian merchant in the medieval epic tale (Bylina),
#. who traveled to the bottom of the sea.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:776
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Sadko"
msgstr "サドコ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:776
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Russian merchant in the medieval epic tale (Bylina), who traveled to the "
"bottom of the sea."
msgstr "中世の叙事詩物語 (ブィリーナ) に登場するロシア商人。海の底まで旅した。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Protagonist in the fiction novel The Underground
#. Railroad, by US author Colson Whitehead (2016). She was a slave who
#. undertook a long journey to freedom in the North through the network of
#. routes and safe houses for fugitive southern slaves, depicted as
#: data/nomenclature.fab:778
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Cora"
msgstr "コーラ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:778
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Protagonist in the fiction novel The Underground Railroad, by US author "
"Colson Whitehead (2016). She was a slave who undertook a long journey to "
"freedom in the North through the network of routes and safe houses for "
"fugitive southern slaves, depicted as"
msgstr ""
"米国作家コルソン・ホワイトヘッドによるフィクション小説『地下鉄道』(2016年) の主人公。 "
"逃亡中の南部奴隷のための通路と隠れ家のネットワークが実際の鉄道として描かれており、彼女は奴隷で、それを使って北部の自由への長い旅を始めた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Greek mythological ship sailed by Jason and his
#. crew, the Argonauts, from Iolcos to Colchis to retrieve the Golden Fleece,
#. described in the "Argonautica" epic poem by Apollonius Rhodius (3rd cen.
#. BC).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:780
msgctxt "chasma"
msgid "Argo Chasma"
msgstr "アルゴ・カズマ地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:780
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Greek mythological ship sailed by Jason and his crew, the Argonauts, from "
"Iolcos to Colchis to retrieve the Golden Fleece, described in the "
"“Argonautica” epic poem by Apollonius Rhodius (3rd cen. BC)."
msgstr ""
"ギリシャ神話でイアソンとアルゴノートと呼ばれる乗員が乗り込んだ帆船、金羊毛を取り戻すため、イオルコスからコルキスへ向かった。アポロニウス・ロディウス "
"(紀元前3世紀) の叙事詩「アルゴナウティカ」に記述がある。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Egyptian boat that carries the sun god Ra across the
#. sky in the daytime.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:782
msgctxt "chasma"
msgid "Mandjet Chasma"
msgstr "マンジェット・カズマ地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:782
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Egyptian boat that carries the sun god Ra across the sky in the daytime."
msgstr "エジプト神話で太陽神ラーを載せて日中に天空を通過する船。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Chilote (southern Chile) legendary, sentient ghost
#. ship, which could suddenly appear and then quickly disappears again,
#. leaving no evidence of its presence.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:784
msgctxt "chasma"
msgid "Caleuche Chasma"
msgstr "カレウチェ・カズマ地形"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:784
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Chilote (southern Chile) legendary, sentient ghost ship, which could "
"suddenly appear and then quickly disappears again, leaving no evidence of "
"its presence."
msgstr "チロテ島 (チリ南部) の知覚力のある伝説の幽霊船、突然現れてすぐに消えてしまい、存在の証拠を残さないこともある。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Anne; US-Irish author of science fiction novels,
#. including the Dragonriders of Pern series, which recounts the human
#. colonization of the fictional planet Pern (1926-2011).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:786
msgctxt "dorsum"
msgid "McCaffrey Dorsum"
msgstr "マキャフリー尾根"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:786
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Anne; US-Irish author of science fiction novels, including the Dragonriders "
"of Pern series, which recounts the human colonization of the fictional "
"planet Pern (1926-2011)."
msgstr ""
"アン; 米国系アイルランド人のSF小説作家 (1926-2011) "
"。代表作に架空の惑星ペルンへの人類の植民地化を描いた『ペルンのドラゴンライダー』シリーズがある。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Stanley, American-British film director and
#. screenwriter (1928-1999). His film "2001: A Space Odyssey" (1968) after the
#. screenplay co-wrote with Arthur Clarke tells the story of humanity’s
#. evolution from tool-using hominids to space explorers and beyon
#: data/nomenclature.fab:788
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Kubrick Mons"
msgstr "キューブリック山"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:788
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Stanley, American-British film director and screenwriter (1928-1999). His "
"film “2001: A Space Odyssey” (1968) after the screenplay co-wrote with "
"Arthur Clarke tells the story of humanity’s evolution from tool-using "
"hominids to space explorers and beyon"
msgstr ""
"スタンリー、アメリカ系イギリス人の映画監督、脚本家 (1928-1999) "
"。アーサー・クラークと共同で脚本を書いた彼の映画『2001年宇宙の旅』（1968年）は、道具を使う原人から宇宙探検家、そしてその先への人類の進化の物語を描いている。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Octavia E., American author (1947-2006). Her
#. "Xenogenesis" trilogy describes humankind’s departure from Earth and
#. subsequent return.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:790
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Butler Mons"
msgstr "バトラー山"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:790
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Octavia E., American author (1947-2006). Her “Xenogenesis” trilogy describes"
" humankind’s departure from Earth and subsequent return."
msgstr ""
"オクタヴィア・E、アメリカの作家 (1947-2006) 。彼女の「ゼノジェネシス」三部作は人類の地球からの出発とその後の帰還を描いている。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Sir Arthur C., British author (1917-2008). Many of
#. his novels depict space explorations, among which the most notable is
#. "2001: A Space Odyssey", describing a voyage to Jupiter. This novel was
#. adapted from the screenplay he co-wrote with Stanley Kubrick
#: data/nomenclature.fab:792
msgctxt "mons"
msgid "Clarke Montes"
msgstr "クラーク山脈"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:792
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Sir Arthur C., British author (1917-2008). Many of his novels depict space "
"explorations, among which the most notable is “2001: A Space Odyssey”, "
"describing a voyage to Jupiter. This novel was adapted from the screenplay "
"he co-wrote with Stanley Kubrick"
msgstr ""
"アーサー・C・卿; イギリスの作家 (1917-2008) "
"。彼の小説の多くは宇宙探検を描いており、その中でも最も注目に値するのは木星への航海を描いた『2001年宇宙の旅』である。この小説はスタンリー・キューブリックと共同で書いた脚本をもとに作られた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Charon); Neverland, a fictional island, the destination of
#. Peter Pan and the Darling children in the 1904 play “Peter Pan; or, The Boy
#. Who Wouldn't Grow Up” and the 1911 novel “Peter and Wendy” by Scottish
#. novelist and dramatist J. M. Barrie (1860-1937).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:794
msgctxt "regio"
msgid "Neverland Regio"
msgstr ""

#: data/nomenclature.fab:794
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Neverland, a fictional island, the destination of Peter Pan and the Darling "
"children in the 1904 play “Peter Pan; or, The Boy Who Wouldn't Grow Up” and "
"the 1911 novel “Peter and Wendy” by Scottish novelist and dramatist J. M. "
"Barrie (1860-1937)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dactyl); One of the original three Dactyls.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:796
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Acmon"
msgstr "アクモン"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:796 data/nomenclature.fab:798
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "One of the original three Dactyls."
msgstr "オリジナルの3匹のダクティルのうちの1匹。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dactyl); One of the original three Dactyls.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:798
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Celmis"
msgstr "ケルミス"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Deimos); Francios-Marie Arouet; French writer (1694-1778).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:800
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Voltaire"
msgstr "ヴォルテール"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:800
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Francios-Marie Arouet; French writer (1694-1778)."
msgstr "フランソワ=マリー・アルエ;  フランスの作家 (1694-1778) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Deimos); Jonathan; British writer (1667-1745).
#. TRANSLATORS: (Moon); Lewis; American astronomer (1820-1913).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:802 data/nomenclature.fab:10912
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Swift"
msgstr "スウィフト"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:802
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Jonathan; British writer (1667-1745)."
msgstr "ジョナサン; イギリスの作家 (1667-1745) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Didymos); Indonesian name of a percussion musical instrument
#. popular in East and South East Asia, a circular metal disk with a definite
#. or indefinite pitch, which is hung vertically and hit in the center by a
#. soft beater; originated in Ancient China.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:804
msgctxt "saxum"
msgid "Gong Saxum"
msgstr "ゴング山塊"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:804
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Indonesian name of a percussion musical instrument popular in East and South"
" East Asia, a circular metal disk with a definite or indefinite pitch, which"
" is hung vertically and hit in the center by a soft beater; originated in "
"Ancient China."
msgstr ""
"東アジアおよび東南アジアで人気のある打楽器のインドネシア語の名前。一定または不定のピッチを持つ円形の金属ディスクが垂直に吊り下げられ、柔らかいビーターで中央を叩く。古代中国に起源を持つ。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Didymos); Belgium, Netherlands, France; a percussion
#. instrument of at least 23 cast bronze bells in fixed suspension.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:806
msgctxt "saxum"
msgid "Carillon Saxum"
msgstr "カリヨン岩塊"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:806
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Belgium, Netherlands, France; a percussion instrument of at least 23 cast "
"bronze bells in fixed suspension."
msgstr "ベルギー、オランダ、フランスの打楽器。少なくとも 23 個の鋳造青銅製の鐘が吊り下げられて固定されている。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); West African gourd-resonated xylophone (Guinea,
#. Senegal, Mali).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:808
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Bala"
msgstr "バラ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:808
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "West African gourd-resonated xylophone (Guinea, Senegal, Mali)."
msgstr "西アフリカ (ガーナ、セネガル、マリ) のひょうたんで共鳴させる木琴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Afro-Cuban; a pair of open bottomed drums played
#. with both hands.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:810
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Bongo"
msgstr "ボンゴ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:810
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Afro-Cuban; a pair of open bottomed drums played with both hands."
msgstr "アフリカ系キューバ人が使う両手で演奏する底開いた一対のドラム。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Percussion musical instrument popular in
#. Guatemala and other Central and NW South American countries; wooden bars
#. with pipe or gourd resonators, struck by yarn wrapped or rubber mallets.
#. Originally developed in Africa.  Marimba was proclaimed the nationa
#: data/nomenclature.fab:812
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Marimba"
msgstr "マリンバ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:812
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Percussion musical instrument popular in Guatemala and other Central and NW "
"South American countries; wooden bars with pipe or gourd resonators, struck "
"by yarn wrapped or rubber mallets. Originally developed in Africa.  Marimba "
"was proclaimed the nationa"
msgstr ""
"グアテマラやその他の中米諸国、南米北西部の諸国で人気のある打楽器; "
"パイプやひょうたんで共鳴させる木の棒を糸を巻いたりゴムで覆った木槌で叩く楽器。元々はアフリカで生まれた。マリンバは国民的楽器とされた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Tanzania; tall cylindrically shaped drum for
#. important rituals, which “drives” the dance.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:814
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Msondo"
msgstr "ムソンド"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:814
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Tanzania; tall cylindrically shaped drum for important rituals, which "
"“drives” the dance."
msgstr "タンザニアの背の高い円筒形の太鼓。重要な儀式で使われ、踊りを「推進」する。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Drum of the Near and Middle East (Iraq, Iran,
#. Turkey), and India; pair of clay or metal kettle drums of various sizes
#. played with curved beaters.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:816
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Naqqara"
msgstr "ネッカラ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:816
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Drum of the Near and Middle East (Iraq, Iran, Turkey), and India; pair of "
"clay or metal kettle drums of various sizes played with curved beaters."
msgstr ""
"近東や中東 (イラク、イラン、トルコ) やインドで使われる太鼓。湾曲したビーターで演奏される、さまざまな大きさの粘土や金属製のケトルドラムのペア。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Uruguay; barrel-shaped drum used to play the
#. Candombe music, a style created by African slaves.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:818
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Tamboril"
msgstr "タンボリル"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:818
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Uruguay; barrel-shaped drum used to play the Candombe music, a style created"
" by African slaves."
msgstr "ウルグアイの樽型の太鼓。アフリカ人奴隷によって生み出されたカンドンベ音楽を演奏するために使用された。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Indian double-headed string-tensioned conical
#. drum.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:820
msgctxt "saxum"
msgid "Dhol Saxum"
msgstr "ドール岩塊"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:820
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Indian double-headed string-tensioned conical drum."
msgstr "インドの双ヘッドで弦を張った円錐ドラム。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Hawaiian small drum with a coconut body and a
#. single sharkskin or fishskin head laced to the bottom.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:822
msgctxt "saxum"
msgid "Pūniu Saxum"
msgstr "プーニ岩塊"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:822
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Hawaiian small drum with a coconut body and a single sharkskin or fishskin "
"head laced to the bottom."
msgstr "ハワイの小さな太鼓。胴体がココナッツで、底にサメの皮、または魚の皮のヘッドが 1 枚編み込まれていまる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Dimorphos); Afro-Brazilian one-headed barrel-shaped drum.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:824
msgctxt "saxum"
msgid "Atabaque Saxum"
msgstr "アタバキ岩塊"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:824
msgctxt "origin"
