msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Tahitian goddess of wisdom, worshipped by the learned."
msgstr "タヒチの知恵の女神、学識者に崇拝された。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Titan); Norse god, the wisest and most eloquent of the Aesir.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:27322
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Forseti"
msgstr "フォルセティ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:27322
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Norse god, the wisest and most eloquent of the Aesir."
msgstr "北欧神話の神、アース神族の中で最も賢明で雄弁。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Titan); Celtic/Irish goddess of water, education, and
#. knowledge. Anyone who drinks the water from her well will become wise.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:27324
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Beag"
msgstr "ビーグ"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:27324
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Celtic/Irish goddess of water, education, and knowledge. Anyone who drinks "
"the water from her well will become wise."
msgstr "ケルト/アイルランドの水、教育、知識の女神。彼女の井戸の水を飲む人は誰でも賢くなる。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Titan); Greek nymph, a minor deity, nurse of the god
#. Dionysus, who instructed him in the Mysteries.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:27326
msgctxt "crater"
msgid "Mystis"
msgstr "ミュスティス"

