msgstr "ローマでのウェスタの巫女 (紀元前420年頃) 。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Alba Longa (usually identified with Castel Gandolfo),
#. in the Alban Hills, 25 km SE of Rome. Ancient city founded by Ascanius.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32214
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Albalonga Catena"
msgstr "アルバロンガ連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32214
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Alba Longa (usually identified with Castel Gandolfo), in the Alban Hills, 25"
" km SE of Rome. Ancient city founded by Ascanius."
msgstr ""
"ローマの南東25kmのアルバン丘陵にあるアルバ・ロンガ (通常はカステル・ガンドルフォと同一視される) 。アスカニウスによって設立された古代都市。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival where a dog was sacrificed to the god
#. Robigus to prevent the red dust, or mildew, which attacked corn when the
#. ear was beginning to form.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32216
msgctxt "catena"
msgid "Robigalia Catena"
msgstr "ロビガリア連鎖クレーター"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32216
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival where a dog was sacrificed to the god Robigus to prevent the "
"red dust, or mildew, which attacked corn when the ear was beginning to form."
msgstr "穂が実り始める時に穀物を襲う赤いほこり、つまり白かび病を防ぐために、神ロビグスに犬を捧げるローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival of the shepherds' and livestocks' god
#. and goddess Pales, held on April 21, feast of purification of the beast,
#. herdsmen, and stalls.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32218
msgctxt "dorsum"
msgid "Parilia Dorsa"
msgstr "パリリア尾根"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32218
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival of the shepherds' and livestocks' god and goddess Pales, held"
" on April 21, feast of purification of the beast, herdsmen, and stalls."
msgstr "4月21日に行われる、羊飼いと家畜の神と女神パレスのローマの祭り。野獣、牧夫、牛舎を浄化する饗宴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival held on July 23 in the heat of the
#. summer to honor Neptunus, god of water.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32220
msgctxt "dorsum"
msgid "Neptunalia Dorsa"
msgstr "ネプチュナリア尾根"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32220
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival held on July 23 in the heat of the summer to honor Neptunus, "
"god of water."
msgstr "水の神ネプチュヌスを称えるため、真夏の7月23日に開催されるローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman city revered it for its Aeneas traditions, its
#. Venus temple, and it cults of Vesta (now Pratica de Mare).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32222
msgctxt "dorsum"
msgid "Lavinium Dorsum"
msgstr "ラウィニウム尾根"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32222
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman city revered it for its Aeneas traditions, its Venus temple, and it "
"cults of Vesta (now Pratica de Mare)."
msgstr "ローマの都市 (現在のプラティカ・デ・マレ) 。アエネアスの伝統やビーナスの神殿、ベスタの信仰を崇敬した。 "

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival reflecting the needs of a small
#. pastoral community, involving the sacrifice of goats and youths striking
#. those whom they met with strips of goat skins, held February 15.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32224
msgctxt "fossa"
msgid "Lupercalia Fossa"
msgstr "ルペルカリア地溝帯"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32224
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival reflecting the needs of a small pastoral community, involving"
" the sacrifice of goats and youths striking those whom they met with strips "
"of goat skins, held February 15."
msgstr "2月15日に開催される、小さな牧畜社会の要求を反映したローマの祭り。ヤギを生け贄に捧げ、若者は出会った人々をヤギの皮で叩く。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival held on December 21 in honor of the
#. goddess Angerona.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32226
msgctxt "fossa"
msgid "Divalia Fossae"
msgstr "ダヴァリア地溝帯"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32226
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Roman festival held on December 21 in honor of the goddess Angerona."
msgstr "12月21日に女神アンゲロナを称えて開催されるローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Three-day Roman festival starting on December 17,
#. with sacrifices, public feasting, gifts, and slaves were waited on by their
#. masters.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32228
msgctxt "fossa"
msgid "Saturnalia Fossae"
msgstr "サートゥルナーリア地溝帯"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32228
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Three-day Roman festival starting on December 17, with sacrifices, public "
"feasting, gifts, and slaves were waited on by their masters."
msgstr "ローマの祭り。12月17日から3日間に渡り、生け贄を捧げ、公の宴会を開き、贈り物が贈られ、主人が奴隷の世話をした。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman All Souls’ Day (February 21) where each
#. household made offerings at the graves of its dead.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32230
msgctxt "planitia"
msgid "Feralia Planitia"
msgstr "フェラリア平原"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32230
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman All Souls’ Day (February 21) where each household made offerings at "
"the graves of its dead."
msgstr "ローマの万霊節 (2月21日) 。各家庭は死者の墓に供物を捧げた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival that included performance of funeral
#. rites, at the first day of the nine-day Parentalia festival honoring
#. ancestors.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32232
msgctxt "rupes"
msgid "Parentatio Rupes"
msgstr "パレンタティオ断崖"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32232
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival that included performance of funeral rites, at the first day "
"of the nine-day Parentalia festival honoring ancestors."
msgstr "祖先を敬う9日間のパレンタリア祭の初日に葬儀の儀式を行う、ローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival celebrated several times a year; on
#. this day the Rex sacrorum offered a ram in the Regia.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32234
msgctxt "rupes"
msgid "Agonium Rupes"
msgstr "アゴニウム断崖"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32234
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival celebrated several times a year; on this day the Rex sacrorum"
" offered a ram in the Regia."
msgstr "年に数回行われるローマの祭り; この日には王が王宮で牡羊を捧げた。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival associated with the goddess Juno,
#. celebrated on March 1.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32236
msgctxt "rupes"
msgid "Matronalia Rupes"
msgstr "マトロナリア断崖"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32236
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival associated with the goddess Juno, celebrated on March 1."
msgstr "3月1日に行われる、女神ユノ (ジュノー) に関連するローマの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival of Vesta, held June 7-15.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32238
msgctxt "terra"
msgid "Vestalia Terra"
msgstr "ウェスタリア大陸"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32238
msgctxt "origin"
msgid "Roman festival of Vesta, held June 7-15."
msgstr "6月7日から15日まで開催されるローマのウェスタ (ヴェスタ) 祭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Roman festival of Bacchus celebrated on the day of
#. the winter solstice.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32240
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Brumalia Tholus"
msgstr "ブルマリア円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32240
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Roman festival of Bacchus celebrated on the day of the winter solstice."
msgstr "冬至の日に祝われるローマのバッカスの祭り。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); Ancient Roman feast held on July 19 when the Romans,
#. defeated and pursued by the Gauls, retired and concealed themselves in the
#. woods.
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32242
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Lucaria Tholus"
msgstr "ルカリア円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32242
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"Ancient Roman feast held on July 19 when the Romans, defeated and pursued by"
" the Gauls, retired and concealed themselves in the woods."
msgstr "7月19日に行われた古代ローマの祭り。ローマ軍がガリア軍に敗れて追撃され、撤退して森の中に身を隠した日。"

#. TRANSLATORS: (Vesta); City at the foot of Albanus Mons, once a powerful
#. city in early Latium (present-day Ariccia).
#: data/nomenclature.fab:32244
msgctxt "tholus"
msgid "Aricia Tholus"
msgstr "アリキア円錐丘"

#: data/nomenclature.fab:32244
msgctxt "origin"
msgid ""
"City at the foot of Albanus Mons, once a powerful city in early Latium "
"(present-day Ariccia)."
msgstr "アルバヌス山の麓にある都市。かつては初期のラティウムあった強力な都市だった。 (現在のアリッチャ) 。"
